    "headingid": 177,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 57048,
        "bookId": 32,
        "chapterId": 37,
        "headingId": 177,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>8525/3 Polymorphous adenocarcinoma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-08-29T17:02:43"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 379,
    "bookid": 32,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 178,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 57049,
        "bookId": 32,
        "chapterId": 37,
        "headingId": 178,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2C60 &amp; XH5SD5 Carcinoma of breast, specialized type &amp; Polymorphous low-grade adenocarcinoma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-08-29T17:02:43"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 380,
    "bookid": 32,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 179,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 57050,
        "bookId": 32,
        "chapterId": 37,
        "headingId": 179,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Not recommended:</em> polymorphous low-grade adenocarcinoma.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-08-29T17:02:43"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 381,
    "bookid": 32,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 180,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 57051,
        "bookId": 32,
        "chapterId": 37,
        "headingId": 180,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-08-29T17:02:43"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 382,
    "bookid": 32,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 181,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 57052,
        "bookId": 32,
        "chapterId": 37,
        "headingId": 181,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>PmA arises in the breast parenchyma, with no site predilection.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-08-29T17:02:43"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 383,
    "bookid": 32,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 182,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 57053,
        "bookId": 32,
        "chapterId": 37,
        "headingId": 182,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>All three of the reported cases presented as palpable nodules affecting adult women aged 37&ndash;74&nbsp;years.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-08-29T17:02:43"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 384,
    "bookid": 32,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 183,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 57054,
        "bookId": 32,
        "chapterId": 37,
        "headingId": 183,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>PmA was originally described in the salivary glands, with a special predilection for the minor salivary glands. Only three cases of breast PmA have been reported to date {16220292}. Therefore, exact data on epidemiology are unavailable.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-08-29T17:02:43"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 385,
    "bookid": 32,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 184,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 57055,
        "bookId": 32,
        "chapterId": 37,
        "headingId": 184,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-08-29T17:02:43"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 386,
    "bookid": 32,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 185,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 57056,
        "bookId": 32,
        "chapterId": 37,
        "headingId": 185,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-08-29T17:02:43"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 393,
    "bookid": 32,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 206,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 57057,
        "bookId": 32,
        "chapterId": 37,
        "headingId": 206,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>PmA presents as parenchymal nodules ranging in size from 1.5 to 4&nbsp;cm.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-08-29T17:02:43"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 387,
    "bookid": 32,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 186,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 57058,
        "bookId": 32,
        "chapterId": 37,
        "headingId": 186,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>At low-power view, PmA is typically composed of a central, large, solid area surrounded by thin strands and cribriform nests of neoplastic cells. The neoplastic cells, which are uniformly small and round, harbour centrally located nucleoli with imperceptible nuclei and a thin rim of pale eosinophilic cytoplasm. Atypical mitotic figures can be detected, whereas coagulation necrosis was not present in the reported cases.</p>\r\n<p>Immunohistochemistry revealed that the neoplastic cells were positive for BCL2. CK7 was only focally positive, and E-cadherin was weakly and partially positive around the cytoplasmic membrane. PmA is negative for ER, PR, and ERBB2 (HER2), with no evidence of <em>ERBB2</em> amplification.</p>\r\n<p>PmA should be differentiated from invasive lobular carcinoma and adenoid cystic carcinoma. PmAs were weakly and focally positive for CK7, markedly positive for BCL2, and negative for ER and PR, in contrast to invasive lobular carcinoma. PmA does not usually have the typical biphasic cellular pattern detected in adenoid cystic carcinoma. PmA is composed of a single cell type, with an absence of myoepithelial and basaloid cells.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-08-29T17:02:43"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 388,
    "bookid": 32,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 187,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 57059,
        "bookId": 32,
        "chapterId": 37,
        "headingId": 187,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-08-29T17:02:43"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 389,
    "bookid": 32,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 188,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 57060,
        "bookId": 32,
        "chapterId": 37,
        "headingId": 188,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>PmA is negative for ER, PR, and HER2, with no evidence of <em>ERBB2</em> amplification.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-08-29T17:02:43"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 392,
    "bookid": 32,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 191,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 57061,
        "bookId": 32,
        "chapterId": 37,
        "headingId": 191,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> typical architectural pattern composed of a centrally located large solid area surrounded by thin strands of uniform and monotonous neoplastic cells.</p>\r\n<p><em>Desirable:</em> focal and weak immunopositivity for CK7 and E-cadherin; negative ER, PR, and HER2.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-08-29T17:02:43"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 390,
    "bookid": 32,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 189,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 57062,
        "bookId": 32,
        "chapterId": 37,
        "headingId": 189,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>PmA is staged according to the criteria adopted for other types of invasive breast carcinomas.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-08-29T17:02:43"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 391,
    "bookid": 32,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 190,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 57063,
        "bookId": 32,
        "chapterId": 37,
        "headingId": 190,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The data reported to date have been insufficient to support definitive conclusions about this tumour, but 1&nbsp;of the 3&nbsp;cases reported {16220292} had widespread metastases resulting in the patient&rsquo;s death 3&nbsp;years after diagnosis. Therefore, as reported for similar neoplasms arising in the salivary glands {28247229}, the term &ldquo;low-grade&rdquo; should not be used for this breast tumour.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2019-08-29T17:02:43"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]